# Merge behaviour for files that are pure append-only registries rather
# than code with logic in it.
#
# The UI barrel is one `export ... from './X'` line per component. Two
# branches adding two different components conflict only because their
# new lines land next to each other — never because the two changes
# actually disagree about anything. `merge=union` keeps both sides'
# lines instead of raising a conflict, which is the right answer in
# every one of those cases.
#
# The tradeoff, accepted deliberately: if two branches do edit the *same*
# line differently, union keeps both versions rather than flagging it.
# That produces a duplicate or contradictory export, which fails
# typecheck and lint immediately — a loud, obvious CI failure, not a
# silently wrong merge. Spurious adjacency is by far the more common
# case here, so trading a rare loud failure for the common silent
# annoyance is worth it.
#
# This only helps where a real git merge runs (locally, and in
# civex-agent's conflict-resolution runner). GitHub's own mergeable
# calculation may still flag the file; the runner pushes the clean merge
# when that happens, which settles it.
frontend/src/components/ui/index.ts merge=union
